## Key Principles

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|-----------------|
| **Zero-diff guarantee** | Use `terraform state mv` *before* refactoring code; resource physical IDs and state data unchanged |
| **Single source of truth** | Environment config in `locals.environments` map; no copy-pasted blocks |
| **Idempotency** | Module parameterizes all differences; dev/prod configs differ only in variable values |
| **Least privilege** | Conditional IAM policies (`enable_least_privilege_role`) enforce prod requirements |
| **Isolation** | Each env in separate module instance; changing prod vars doesn't touch dev state |
| **Scalability** | Adding a third environment (`staging`) requires only one new entry in `locals.environments` |

---

## Common Pitfalls & Fixes

| Pitfall | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| State move typo causes resource to be recreated | Always dry-run moves: `terraform state list` before `state mv` |
| Changing resource names in module breaks state | Use identical names in module (`aws_eks_cluster.main` not `aws_eks_cluster.cluster`) |
| Forgetting to move all dependent resources | Use `terraform state list` to find all old resource addresses |
| Applying before all moves complete | Run `terraform plan` after *all* moves; should show zero changes |
| Module conditional (`count`/`for_each`) logic breaks state | Pre-compute conditions in root module; pass boolean flags to module |

